Robert den Hartog (robert@popeye.gen.nz) wrote:
: Questions:  I've found(and killed) two Angel who didn't like me, even though
: I was lucky and piously alligned.  They seemed to be capable of up to 50hp
: damage per attack hits (from around 160HP, AC -12).  Why dont they like me?
: (One told me I was unworthy and that I will soon meet my maker.) I won luckily
: (and picked up a blessed rustproof +2 long sword - good spare weapon.)
: No corpse was left (from two Angels), I guess that might be ok.  Did I do
: any damage to my alighnment by killing them?  It is possible for a corpse to
: be left, and if so would it be worth (or wise) to eat it?

This gives a good idea for new armor/cloak/ability: flying.  Some
monsters have this ability: Vampires, bees... If you kill an angel
perhaps they would leave wings behind.  If you wore them (as a cloak) and
read an enchant armor scroll they would turn into a cloak of flying.

Flying is different from levitating because you can reach the floor while
flying.

: Another question: can I disable a trap door in any way (I was thinking of
: pushing a boulder it it, will it work?), and why do the items over a trap
: door, or a hole dug by a wand of digging/pickaxe not fall through?  At least
: in the latter case this should happen.

1) A boulder will do the trick
2) things sometime DO fall in.  Try throwing items at a trap door that is
against the wall.  When the item hits the wall and stops, it drops to the
ground sometimes knocking other items in.

: Final question (for now).  What use was the oracle?  I paid him twice and got
: some useless information (about as useful as talking to a shop keeper).  Later
: I killed him/her.  Have I lost something now?  Also I tried applying an orb
: I picked up in the gnomish mines and it exploded, another mistake?

1) The oracle is good for major consultations.  Sometimes they give you
really useful information.  Killing them is a mistake.

2) The orb probably exploded because it was cursed or you have very low
intelligence or perhaps both.

